"Spectral properties of random graphs with fixed equitable partition (https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.07675)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.0 years ago; Title: Spectral properties of random graphs with fixed equitable partition ... An $S$-regular matrix is defined then as a matrix on an $S$-regular graph consistent with the graph's equitable partition.\nTitle: Spectral properties of random graphs with fixed equitable partition\nAuthors: Matthew B. Crawford, David J. Marchette, William Maxwell, Samuel S. Mendelson\nDate: Mon Nov 13 19:01:40 2023\n\nWe define a graph to be $S$-regular if it contains an equitable partition given by a matrix $S$. These graphs are generalizations of both regular and bipartite, biregular graphs. An $S$-regular matrix is defined then as a matrix on an $S$-regular graph consistent with the graph's equitable partition. In this paper we derive the limiting spectral density for large, random $S$-regular matrices as well as limiting functions of certain statistics for their eigenvector coordinates as a function of eigenvalue. These limiting functions are defined in terms of spectral measures on $S$-regular trees. In general, these spectral measures do not have a closed-form expression; however, we provide a defining system of polynomials for them. Finally, we explore eigenvalue bounds of $S$-regular graph, proving an expander mixing lemma, Alon-Bopana bound, and other eigenvalue inequalities in terms of the eigenvalues of the matrix $S$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFull article: Spatial maxima, unimodality, and asymptotic behaviour of solutions to discrete diffusion-type equations (https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10236198.2022.2027395)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; According to [Citation4, Theorem 4.7], the convolution of two symmetric discrete unimodal distributions is unimodal. ... The proof is simple, but r